  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Marine Plastics Monitor",
    "description": "A survey input assistant platform developed for Clean Oceans International. Clean Oceans International is a non-profit organization that uses a survey protocol to collect data about the plastic debris building up on our shores. The Marine Plastics Monitor is a website with a companion mobile app that has digitized the survey process to invite more citizen scientists to participate in data collection. The website offers data visualization for the plastic data that has been collected at a number of beaches. \nMy contribution to the website involved improving pre-existing data visuals, adding more robust functionality to the map, implementing a review system for a survey, and various bug fixes for the previous functionality. On the mobile app, I developed the survey input functionality, worked on the submission of a survey by adding in input validation, and implemented a local storage and developed functionalities similar to MongoDB queries.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Jan 2019 - Jul 2019"
   },
   {
    "title": "Dining Slug",
    "description": "Website (if available: www.diningslug.com)\nThis was a three month project that I worked on with five other developers to improve upon the university's current dining hall website. It allows users to search for specific menu items as well as rate the food and monitor each dining hall's capacity. I helped to develop the front end portion of the website using React.js as well as built a portion of the website's back end using Node.js and Express",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Sep 2018 - Dec 2018"
   }
